T1 run A · stage 1a · 2026-09-12 · commit fbe3901 — the Claim exit, DERO simulator with simhtlc's fake Monero wallet
====================================================================================================================
Plan: docs/MAINNET_TEST_PLAN.md §6 T1, stage 1a, first command. Machine paths are written <repo>, <tmp>, <user>.
This run is evidence about the DERO side only: the Monero side is the in-process fake monero-wallet-rpc.

Command (from <repo>/tools; simhtlc built with go1.26.8 at fbe3901; below-normal priority):
  go run ./simhtlc -fake-monero -prover "wsl.exe -e <path to the pinned proof-xmr build>" -paths happy -state-dir <tmp>/st/t1-fake
The plan's command plus -state-dir, so that the state files could be read afterwards (§4); the default is a temporary
directory. Every other flag at simhtlc's default (-h at fbe3901): -t1 48 -t2 20 -t1-min 10 -t2-min 6 -stable 2
-confs 10 -gate-deadline 4 -claim-margin 2 -fee 2000 -amount-dero 2000 -amount-xmr 1000000000000 -stipend 14016, and an
htlc.bas v3 of its own at -htlc-w1min 10 -htlc-w2min 6 -htlc-g2 30. The prover: the reproducible proof-xmr build in WSL,
whose sha256 was read as 7293e9c97e0330966499fff397a0488ef40d38f65da49423429c8c548c83d39d before the stage.

